#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100672 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7fab292c-d43d-50bb-b785-f1e15122c6c7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Position Vector in Component Form"}] :question/id #uuid "1985c614-4597-521c-bb2d-289fab264708" :question/math-academy-id "e-4289" :question/problem "Find the position vector of $A(-1,2)$ in terms of $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf{j}$." :question/worked-solution "Our vector is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/26/269326f4375dfad6d05e4468f4831012bde4a57bc85fbdfc7082cc466d3522dd.png)\n\nRemember that in general, if a point $A$ has coordinates $(a_x,a_y)$, then its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OA} = a_x\\mathbf{i}+a_y\\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\nHere, the point $A$ has coordinates $(-1,2)$, so its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nOA^(→) &= (-1) \\cdot i + 2 \\cdot j \\\\\n&=-i + 2j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100674 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100855 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63fc6e25-89d7-56fb-bd4c-a4b5637b7711" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Position Vector in Angle Bracket Notation"}] :question/id #uuid "ad6fec65-5309-58e4-b899-3302188f0e91" :question/math-academy-id "e-4290" :question/problem "The points $A, B, C$, and $O$ are shown in the picture below. Find the corresponding position vectors, using angle bracket notation.\n\n![](images/92/92eb1531e0e5e308edb85da62149a220166c8bd37fc0f66d600e9a9599731195.png)" :question/worked-solution "For a point with coordinates $(a_x, a_y)$, the position vector is\n\n$$\n\\left< a_x, a_y \\right>\n$$\n\n- The point $A$ has coordinates $(-1,2)$, so the position vector is\n$\\overrightarrow{OA} = \\langle -1,2 \\rangle$.\n- The point $B$ has coordinates $(3, 1.5)$, so the position vector is\n$\\overrightarrow{OB} = \\langle 3, 1.5 \\rangle$.\n- The point $C$ has coordinates $(1,-2)$, so the position vector is\n$\\overrightarrow{OC} = \\langle 1,-2 \\rangle$.\n- The point $O$ has coordinates $(0,0)$, so the position vector is\n$\\overrightarrow{OO} = \\langle 0,0 \\rangle = \\mathbf{0}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100675 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49e90ac1-2e90-51de-831b-a061b4ee80ad" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector in Component Form"}] :question/id #uuid "ed5a0713-9dec-5f91-ae4f-26dcc25ef174" :question/math-academy-id "e-4291" :question/problem "Let $A(-2,1)$ and $B(2,3)$. Find $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ in terms of $\\mathbf{i}$ and $\\mathbf{j}$." :question/worked-solution "Our vector is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/76/76c98067c9780e9c903dda8657b67a2db473ecd8ef24e53e2262ba2f46a4293a.png)\n\nWe have\n\n$$\nOA^(→) = a =-2i + j,; OB^(→) = b = 2i + 3j\n$$\n\nNow, from $\\triangle OAB$, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAB^(→) &= AO^(→) + OB^(→) \\\\\n&=-OA^(→) + OB^(→) \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (2i + 3j) - (-2i + j) \\\\\n&= 4i + 2j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573254 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49e90ac1-2e90-51de-831b-a061b4ee80ad" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector in Component Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0918aa6f-d79a-59b7-b036-f09c09d416f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4i+3j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572835} {:answer/id #uuid "119b7c67-105f-57b9-84ad-4013cc89578f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572843} {:answer/id #uuid "3d93145f-15ca-53ac-a097-c6809b88a220" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572892} {:answer/id #uuid "63fba524-5aa2-55e9-886f-823f761a35cf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3i+4j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572943} {:answer/id #uuid "aff6f09b-1196-5e20-a457-23bfa327b5e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2i-j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573048}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "119b7c67-105f-57b9-84ad-4013cc89578f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572843} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed18c90b-b986-5dce-aa2a-f3fbde5655b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573240}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "092e8310-501d-5972-983c-e6366efca630" :question/math-academy-id "q-124990" :question/problem "![](images/cc/ccb8643e7dfde7aa26d290c5f6e49a2037f37594bc05c558c46dea6bd673d9ff.png)\n\nLet $A(1,1)$ and $B(3,2).$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ in terms of $i$ and $j.$" :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=i+j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=3i+2j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from $△OAB$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =b-a \\\\  & =(3i+2j)-(i+j) \\\\  & =2i+j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573269 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100855 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63fc6e25-89d7-56fb-bd4c-a4b5637b7711" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Position Vector in Angle Bracket Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f8e4fb1-e97d-5d7e-9e20-606f4bacf723" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=⟨-2.5,1.5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572859} {:answer/id #uuid "6ccf55a3-a4eb-5a92-bc90-105041733e42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=⟨1.5,-2.5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572958} {:answer/id #uuid "a1e3cede-7915-55a0-9ff3-f726b6d6c5ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=⟨-1,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573030} {:answer/id #uuid "a33fbd40-fc91-5b05-9f63-429460e594bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=⟨1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573032} {:answer/id #uuid "cece7db9-017d-561e-86f1-e814f9065dd4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=⟨2.5,-1.5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6ccf55a3-a4eb-5a92-bc90-105041733e42" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OW}=⟨1.5,-2.5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572958} :answer-field/id #uuid "e09e382f-322a-5a58-807a-349de626a047" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573236}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "33670b3f-b9d2-5fe2-ab57-0eab9223a358" :question/math-academy-id "q-17993" :question/problem "![](images/a8/a86e5e973e15230943beaa3f8afdeed139690ba4e5cf3fed4c35895e5f4bd2d4.png)\n\nThe point $W$ is shown in the picture above. Find the coordinates of the corresponding position vector." :question/worked-solution "For a point with coordinates $({a}_{x},{a}_{y}),$ the position vector is $⟨{a}_{x},{a}_{y}⟩.$\n\nThe point $W$ has coordinates $(1.5,-2.5),$ so the position vector is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OW}=⟨1.5,-2.5⟩.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573286 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49e90ac1-2e90-51de-831b-a061b4ee80ad" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector in Component Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5637e942-8fdc-5683-97b7-4c85a13c3f1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5i+2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572923} {:answer/id #uuid "7d07658d-e91e-5270-bab5-3abea0cac458" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5i+2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572985} {:answer/id #uuid "cf15061c-1d9b-591f-9ac9-80c350b0c96e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5i-2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573086} {:answer/id #uuid "f05d338a-26b3-50a3-a01d-778bfd91e38b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5i-3j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573130} {:answer/id #uuid "f6158f2a-fa36-56c6-9c28-fd2a7c586f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5i-2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f6158f2a-fa36-56c6-9c28-fd2a7c586f5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5i-2j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573135} :answer-field/id #uuid "8cc93057-1e5d-5bac-8670-57949bf9620b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573200}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "72c863fb-10f9-5099-ad8d-1290ffd2a6a9" :question/math-academy-id "q-18000" :question/problem "![](images/84/84d2c65b53d4095bc3501f9658f2ff597dd9b72fff6e5e2b5b7347834632dfac.png)\n\nLet $A(2,0)$ and $B(-3,-2).$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ in terms of $i$ and $j.$" :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=2i+0j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=-3i-2j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from $△OAB$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =b-a \\\\  & =(-3i-2j)-(2i+0j) \\\\  & =-5i-2j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573321 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100856 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "49e90ac1-2e90-51de-831b-a061b4ee80ad" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Vector in Component Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e0ba453-1215-5b3d-a7f0-05c27ba16c19" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572895} {:answer/id #uuid "6409fd64-52ae-588b-83ba-95d3807aaa0a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572944} {:answer/id #uuid "940aeb78-c446-5984-88ec-716288861a2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573015} {:answer/id #uuid "d383c3fb-fbe1-569b-ac8c-3692a5c7d2e5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "i+3j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573093} {:answer/id #uuid "f2e6b0be-7712-5a3d-8735-6c39db9d2f2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2i+j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573133}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "940aeb78-c446-5984-88ec-716288861a2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573015} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed7ddc08-5f8d-5c40-bda9-117726299567" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573241}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0302994-59bc-5fe6-beeb-f786801b16b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-18003" :question/problem "![](images/94/944c91a9d428f3b84cd748d40da9178b494522a5b39777fe0b8e875f9733f537.png)\n\nLet $A(-1,2)$ and $B(-1,3).$ Find $\\overset{\\to }{AB}$ in terms of $i$ and $j.$" :question/worked-solution "We have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\overset{\\to }{OA}=a=-i+2j, \\\\  & \\overset{\\to }{OB}=b=-i+3j.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, from $△OAB$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =\\overset{\\to }{AO}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =-\\overset{\\to }{OA}+\\overset{\\to }{OB} \\\\  & =b-a \\\\  & =(-i+3j)-(-i+2j) \\\\  & =0i+j \\\\  & =j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573291 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7fab292c-d43d-50bb-b785-f1e15122c6c7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Position Vector in Component Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f838cae-7963-53d4-adb3-055a400661b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f838cae-7963-53d4-adb3-055a400661b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572898} :answer-field/id #uuid "17341d17-b542-5bd7-8870-0b8622258187" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573155} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ef63d38a-802f-5985-9655-3a158ab709d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ef63d38a-802f-5985-9655-3a158ab709d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573129} :answer-field/id #uuid "980f9f0e-eb5c-5ec7-abf3-93c02c0e570a" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573207}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f6ad506-8ae9-5d30-a511-9a3173b92b8c" :question/math-academy-id "q-275102" :question/problem "Find the position vector of $R(-4,5)$ in terms of $i$ and $j.$\n\nThe position vector of $R$ is\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j.$" :question/worked-solution "Our vector is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/e1/e132f8e20ffb38c70ef435a560a584b25a6509486cc148636d873a9e0e94ea52.png)\n\nRemember that in general, if a point $R$ has coordinates $({r}_{x},{r}_{y}),$ then its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OR}={r}_{x}i+{r}_{y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nHere, the point $R$ has coordinates $(-4,5),$ so its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OR} & =(-4)\\cdot i+5\\cdot j \\\\  & =-4\\,i+5\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573322 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100854 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7fab292c-d43d-50bb-b785-f1e15122c6c7" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Position Vector in Component Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2eb75c7d-58aa-5163-a4e4-40ddb2a2085f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572875}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2eb75c7d-58aa-5163-a4e4-40ddb2a2085f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572875} :answer-field/id #uuid "f238910f-e8b0-53f4-b405-ed0629614fa4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573243} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "552b7b0f-082f-543f-9e21-d944b2bef379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "552b7b0f-082f-543f-9e21-d944b2bef379" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572922} :answer-field/id #uuid "f51c13dd-8656-5d5a-bd3b-d888aad6056e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573246}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f1d56472-7ebb-55ed-bd03-c4b2a70fb522" :question/math-academy-id "q-316790" :question/problem "Find the position vector of $R(2,4)$ in terms of $i$ and $j.$\n\nThe position vector of $R$ is\n{{field-1}}\n$i\\,\\,+$\n{{field-2}}\n$j.$" :question/worked-solution "Our vector is shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/ec/ecc6f3682d17eb4878e43a24ada2d6989d73f34d44ce2e3adcf9e6dc201761d2.png)\n\nRemember that in general, if a point $R$ has coordinates $({r}_{x},{r}_{y}),$ then its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OR}={r}_{x}i+{r}_{y}\\,j.\n$$\n\nHere, the point $R$ has coordinates $(2,4),$ so its position vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{OR} & =2\\,i+4\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186573299 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100855 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "63fc6e25-89d7-56fb-bd4c-a4b5637b7711" :knowledge-point/title "Expressing a Position Vector in Angle Bracket Notation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "26f374cf-1d35-55d4-8591-b25423346911" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OU}=⟨-3,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572871} {:answer/id #uuid "3a972473-034b-5cb5-b1d8-f2259eeea6c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OU}=⟨3,2.5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572887} {:answer/id #uuid "46660aed-b32f-53d3-bbab-ea705491f7b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OU}=⟨2.5,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572911} {:answer/id #uuid "698a014e-add4-5f36-8c6a-bc365e637fcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OU}=⟨3,-2.5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572953} {:answer/id #uuid "b9cca592-116e-5655-9b6f-742a081eb34b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OU}=⟨3,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573061}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a972473-034b-5cb5-b1d8-f2259eeea6c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\overset{\\to }{OU}=⟨3,2.5⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186572887} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d12eb5-b989-5e71-915d-c112ac4d08f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186573230}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "adab0e55-06f3-58c6-9e94-4deec9447e84" :question/math-academy-id "q-70514" :question/problem "![](images/64/64d06368521604c208208a9d72452282f1ee8e683257ed9cd0161e957e39173c.png)\n\nThe point $U$ is shown in the picture above. Find the coordinates of the corresponding position vector." :question/worked-solution "For a point with coordinates $({a}_{x},{a}_{y}),$ the position vector is $⟨{a}_{x},{a}_{y}⟩.$\n\nThe point $U$ has coordinates $(3,2.5),$ so the position vector is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{OU}=⟨3,2.5⟩.\n$$"}]}
